cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Sheep Brain Study Guide
message: >-
  If you use this module in your teaching or reference it in
  scholarship, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "FlowingMind"
    # Add a personal author alongside the org if you'd prefer to be cited by name:
    # - given-names: ""
    #   family-names: ""
    #   affiliation: "St. Mary's College of Maryland"
    #   orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/torryscott/sheepbrain"
abstract: >-
  A customizable neuroanatomy practicum for Qualtrics. Students
  identify structures on photographs of a preserved sheep brain
  across three anatomical views. Instructors select which
  structures are included via URL parameters, without editing or
  duplicating the survey. Includes an interactive labeled atlas
  with keyboard- and screen-reader-accessible study modes.
keywords:
  - neuroanatomy
  - anatomy education
  - Qualtrics
  - sheep brain
  - interactive atlas
  - open educational resources
license: MIT
